Scenario:

Two students have selected different subjects. Write a Java program using retainAll() to find the subjects common to both students.

Program:

import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Set;

public class CommonSubjects {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Set<String> student1 = new HashSet<>();
        Set<String> student2 = new HashSet<>();

        student1.add("Java");
        student1.add("Python");
        student1.add("Database");
        student1.add("C++");

        student2.add("Java");
        student2.add("Database");
        student2.add("Networking");
        student2.add("HTML");

        System.out.println("Student 1 Subjects: " + student1);
        System.out.println("Student 2 Subjects: " + student2);

        student1.retainAll(student2);

        System.out.println("Common Subjects: " + student1);
    }
}

Output:

Student 1 Subjects: [Java, Python, Database, C++]
Student 2 Subjects: [Java, Database, Networking, HTML]
Common Subjects: [Java, Database]
